  "notes": "Double-sided 22-position edge connector drawn as A|1 ... Z|22. Each side carries its own label: the label left of the letter column belongs to the letter contact, the label right of the number column to the number contact, so letter and number contacts are recorded as separate pins (also = opposite contact). Pairs drawn on both sides (J/8 PREAMP OUT, P/13 OUTPUT AMP SUPPLY, Y/21 SPKR OUT, Z/22 OUTPUT AMP COM) look like the same signal bussed on both faces. No polarity marked on any audio pair; port keys a/b are drawn order. Supply voltages not stated. 'Output amp in' shield assumed to be T (SHIELD next to U/V) and preamp in shield 5 (SHIELD next to 3/4) by position. Legend: NC = not connected. Same drawing as the other M703B scan in this folder."
